diff --git a/purpose/kits/validation/README.md b/purpose/kits/validation/README.md
index 192eb13a..60a80fb7 100644
--- a/purpose/kits/validation/README.md
+++ b/purpose/kits/validation/README.md
@@ -12,3 +12,27 @@ Purpose layer, second kit (EE-026). How probable it is that a venture is validat
 | References | `references/references.json` |
 
 Sub-scores: problem, solution, product-market fit, pricing, go-to-market, team, operations readiness per MAD tier.
+
+## Discovery interviews
+
+Recruiting founders, preparing for each conversation and keeping the outreach log, before the interview itself is filed in `validation/interviews/`. `schema/discovery.ts` runs it; `schema/discovery-test.ts` tests it.
+
+| Record | Where | Holds |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Lead, then prospect | `validation/discovery/leads/<person>.json` | everyone imported is a lead (status `new`); a person qualifies one and it becomes a prospect (`qualified_by`). Agents may draft a `fit` rank, never qualify. It holds an opaque person id (`p-xxxx`), the ICP, how they were found (own network, community, cold), their money stage, the outreach log |
+| Contact (private) | `_private/people/<person>.json` | the real name, profile link, email and company; `private: true`, so it never reaches a model or a release |
+| Dossier | `validation/discovery/dossiers/<person>.json` | facts about the founder and their venture, each with a public source, each a draft until a person checks it |
+| Meeting | `validation/discovery/meetings/<id>.json` | the time, the script tagged to H1, H2 and the price anchor, the prediction written before it, then the recording's raw source, the interview filed from it and the introduction asked for |
+
+```sh
+node schema/discovery.ts import <venture> Connections.csv --icp <icp id> --match founder
+node schema/discovery.ts plan <venture> --person <p-id> --at 2026-11-03T15:00:00-06:00 --prediction "..."
+node schema/discovery.ts packet <venture> <meeting id> [--names]
+node schema/discovery.ts funnel <venture>
+node schema/discovery.ts check <venture>
+```
+
+- `import` reads the founder's own official LinkedIn data export (Connections.csv). Nothing fetches LinkedIn. The export's columns are inferred from public descriptions; check them against a real export.
+- `check` fails a dossier fact an agent sourced from a linkedin.com page, a fact confirmed by the agent that compiled it, a dossier, lead or meeting that names the person, a script that pitches Naive, Mentura, the puzzle or the waitlist or asks a hypothetical price, and a held meeting with no prediction.
+- The packet is a view rebuilt from the records. It keeps checked facts apart from drafts and shows every fact's source. With `--names` it reads `_private/`, so keep that copy off any model.
+
