@@ -41,3 +41,12 @@ When the evidence supports the commitment the founder is about to make. Prototyp
 
 - Never invent evidence or fill a source with a plausible URL. A missing source is an open question.
 - Interview notes may hold personal data. Keep names out of the notes, or keep the notes out of any public repository.
+
+## Recruiting and preparing interviews
+
+When the cheapest evidence is interviews, run them through the discovery records (`purpose/kits/validation/README.md`, Discovery interviews):
+
+- Import leads from the founder's own LinkedIn export with `node schema/discovery.ts import <venture> Connections.csv --icp <icp id>`. Never read LinkedIn pages yourself. A lead has only a person id; the name stays in `_private/people/`, which you never read or quote.
+- Write a dossier as drafts, each fact with a public source. Only a person marks a fact confirmed.
+- Plan the meeting with `node schema/discovery.ts plan`, and ask the founder for a prediction before it. Never add a question that pitches the product or asks what they would pay.
+- Run `node schema/discovery.ts check <venture>` before you hand over a packet (`node schema/discovery.ts packet <venture> <meeting id>`).
